         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### One of the First\n\nWhen they were digging at the archaeological site of Caral, in Peru, researchers found what may be one of the oldest counting systems created by humanity: the quipus.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p class=\"desc\"><img src=\"https://www.historytracers.org/images/Caral/QuipuPanel.png\" class=\"imgcenter\"/><b>Figure 1</b>: Panel at the archaeological site of Caral showing a person holding a quipu and a Yupana board.</p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
