               }
            },
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "b74bf294-c758-4a48-88c9-399ca4f021f6",
               "text": "Cartwright, M.",
               "page": "https://www.worldhistory.org/Quipu/",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2014",
                  "month": "05",
                  "day": "08"
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nIn this class, we learned about the quipu, a decimal numerical system that was used in the Andes, possibly for thousands of years.\n\nLike the numbers we use every day, a quipu can represent any number. But instead of adding digits to the left, the quipumakers continued adding knots on top.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
